---
import OnboardingLayout from "../layout/onboardinglayout.astro";
---

<OnboardingLayout active="misc">
  <div class="w-[92%] md:w-[70%] mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-[6vw] md:text-[2.6vw] font-black tracking-tight">
      Executive Board Onboarding
    </h1>

    <span class="mt-[1.2vw] inline-block rounded bg-orange-100 px-[1vw] py-[0.5vw] md:px-[0.5vw] md:py-[0.2vw] text-[2.3vw] md:text-[0.75vw] text-orange-800">
      Last updated April 23, 2026
    </span>

    <!-- Tabs -->
    <div class="mt-[4vw] md:mt-[1.6vw] flex items-center gap-[4vw] md:gap-[1.6vw] border-b border-black/10 pb-[2vw] md:pb-[0.6vw]">
      <button class="flex items-center gap-[1vw] md:gap-[0.4vw] text-[3vw] md:text-[0.9vw] font-semibold text-black">
        <!-- External link icon -->
        <svg class="w-[3.5vw] md:w-[1vw] h-[3.5vw] md:h-[1vw]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 6H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 003 8.25v10.5A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h10.5A2.25 2.25 0 0018 18.75V10.5m-10.5 6L21 3m0 0h-5.25M21 3v5.25" />
        </svg>
        Links
      </button>
      <button class="flex items-center gap-[1vw] md:gap-[0.4vw] text-[3vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/40">
        <!-- Envelope icon -->
        <svg class="w-[3.5vw] md:w-[1vw] h-[3.5vw] md:h-[1vw]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M21.75 6.75v10.5a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.25 2.25h-15a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.25-2.25V6.75m19.5 0A2.25 2.25 0 0019.5 4.5h-15a2.25 2.25 0 00-2.25 2.25m19.5 0v.243a2.25 2.25 0 01-1.07 1.916l-7.5 4.615a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.36 0L3.32 8.91a2.25 2.25 0 01-1.07-1.916V6.75" />
        </svg>
        Key Contacts
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Content area -->
    <div class="mt-[4vw] md:mt-[1.6vw]">
      <h3 class="text-[4vw] md:text-[1.2vw] font-bold">Welcome to the Executive Board</h3>
      <p class="mt-[1.6vw] md:mt-[0.6vw] text-[2.8vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
        As an executive board member of IEEE at UC San Diego, you steer the direction of the organization and support every chair and general officer under your branch. You are the bridge between the general body, UCSD departments (AS, CSI, SLBO, ECE, CSE), and IEEE's larger San Diego Section. This page covers the shared expectations for President, VC Internal, VC External, VC Events, VC Finance, VC Operations, and VC Projects.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Overview -->
    <div class="mt-[6vw] md:mt-[2.4vw] flex items-center gap-[1.4vw] md:gap-[0.5vw] border-b border-black/10 pb-[2vw] md:pb-[0.6vw]">
      <!-- Info circle icon -->
      <svg class="w-[3.5vw] md:w-[1vw] h-[3.5vw] md:h-[1vw] text-black/70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.25 11.25l.041-.02a.75.75 0 011.063.852l-.708 2.836a.75.75 0 001.063.853l.041-.021M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0zm-9-3.75h.008v.008H12V8.25z" />
      </svg>
      <span class="text-[3vw] md:text-[0.9vw] font-semibold">Overview</span>
    </div>

    <!-- External Entities -->
    <h2 class="mt-[6vw] md:mt-[2.4vw] text-[5vw] md:text-[2vw] font-black tracking-tight">
      Executive Responsibilities
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-[4vw] md:mt-[1.6vw] space-y-[6vw] md:space-y-[2.4vw]">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[4vw] md:text-[1.3vw] font-bold">1. Main Tasks of the Position</h3>
        <ul class="mt-[2vw] md:mt-[0.6vw] list-disc pl-[4vw] md:pl-[1.4vw] space-y-[1vw] md:space-y-[0.3vw] text-[2.8vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
            <li>Lead, mentor, and coordinate the chairs under your branch (Events, Finance, Internal, External, Operations, Projects).</li>
            <li>Set and enforce quarterly goals across event cadence, funding targets, outreach milestones, and project deliverables.</li>
            <li>Attend all All-Hands meetings, weekly exec syncs, and branch-specific meetings; follow up with your chairs in between.</li>
            <li>Approve event requests, budgets, and funding applications on the IEEE dashboard before they go to AS or TAP.</li>
            <li>Represent IEEE at UCSD to external partners: AS, CSI, SLBO, ECE/CSE departments, IEEE San Diego Section, sponsors, and other orgs.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[4vw] md:text-[1.3vw] font-bold">2. External Entities You Work With</h3>
        <ul class="mt-[2vw] md:mt-[0.6vw] list-disc pl-[4vw] md:pl-[1.4vw] space-y-[1vw] md:space-y-[0.3vw] text-[2.8vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>AS (Associated Students):</strong> funds food and sometimes materials. Primary contact: Chris. Submit Programming Apps 5 weeks ahead and PEEFs after each event.</li>
            <li><strong>SLBO (Student Life Business Office):</strong> handles purchases, expenses, and reimbursements. Primary contact: Alma via TAP or email.</li>
            <li><strong>CSI (Center for Student Involvement):</strong> advisor for non-food, non-money matters (policy, risk, conduct). Primary contact: Maria.</li>
            <li><strong>IEEE San Diego Section:</strong> external funding via VTools for academically oriented events (workshops, GBMs, outreach).</li>
            <li><strong>ECE &amp; CSE Departments:</strong> room bookings (Jacobs Hall / EBU1, Henry Booker Room, Qualcomm Conference Room) and newsletter promotion.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[4vw] md:text-[1.3vw] font-bold">3. Principal Members &amp; Approvals</h3>
        <ul class="mt-[2vw] md:mt-[0.6vw] list-disc pl-[4vw] md:pl-[1.4vw] space-y-[1vw] md:space-y-[0.3vw] text-[2.8vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
            <li>Every exec is a <strong>Principal Member</strong> on TAP and can front reimbursements for AS-funded events.</li>
            <li>Only use a Principal Member's card for AS-funded purchases. Never use a personal card from a non-PM.</li>
            <li>Submit reimbursements <strong>within 7 days</strong> of the event. Coordinate with VC Operations and VC Finance to track outstanding payments.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[4vw] md:text-[1.3vw] font-bold">4. Quarterly Cadence</h3>
        <ul class="mt-[2vw] md:mt-[0.6vw] list-disc pl-[4vw] md:pl-[1.4vw] space-y-[1vw] md:space-y-[0.3vw] text-[2.8vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Pre-quarter:</strong> set the event calendar, confirm budgets, assign chairs to events, and lock in the kickoff GBM date.</li>
            <li><strong>Weeks 1&ndash;2:</strong> tabling (Library Walk, Engineering on the Green), kickoff GBM, project team applications open.</li>
            <li><strong>Weeks 3&ndash;9:</strong> ongoing workshops, socials, workathons, and project meetings. Monitor event submissions and reimbursement turnaround.</li>
            <li><strong>Week 10 / Finals:</strong> wrap up reimbursements, post recaps, run a retro with your branch, and prepare transition notes for next quarter.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[4vw] md:text-[1.3vw] font-bold">5. Advice From Past Execs</h3>
        <ul class="mt-[2vw] md:mt-[0.6vw] list-disc pl-[4vw] md:pl-[1.4vw] space-y-[1vw] md:space-y-[0.3vw] text-[2.8vw] md:text-[0.9vw] text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
            <li>Document everything: vendor contacts, room confirmations, and decisions. The next exec will thank you.</li>
            <li>Get <strong>written</strong> confirmations for room bookings and food orders before the event date.</li>
            <li>Delegate early. Your chairs want responsibility, so don't be the bottleneck for every decision.</li>
            <li>Respond to AS and TAP deadlines the day they land; slippage compounds fast.</li>
            <li>Hold monthly 1:1s with each of your chairs to catch burnout and blockers before they become problems.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</OnboardingLayout>
